Instruction: Read the following excerpt from a Transaction Agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.

Question: Is the ‘ability to efficiently finalize the transaction’ provision subject to Material Adverse Effect carveouts?
Option A: No
Option B: Yes

Transaction Agreement Excerpt:
"Acquisition Material Impact" shall mean any change, occurrence, or series of occurrences that materially adversely affects the financial performance, operations, or ability of the Acquired Entity to complete the Transaction in a timely manner. Such Impact shall include any event that, individually or in aggregate, delays or impairs completion; however, notwithstanding the foregoing, the following events shall not be deemed to cause an Acquisition Material Impact:
   (i) Fluctuations in general economic conditions or capital market volatility that similarly affect industry peers;
   (ii) Increases in interest rates, exchange rates, or credit ratings occurring after execution of this Agreement, provided they do not uniquely disadvantage the Acquired Entity;
   (iii) Regulatory or statutory changes, including alterations in accounting standards, whose effects are comparable to those experienced by competitors;
   (iv) Force majeure events such as natural disasters, pandemics, or geopolitical conflicts, so long as their adverse effects are not disproportionate relative to industry comparators;
   (v) Any adverse effect arising solely from public or private announcements regarding this Agreement or the Transaction.
Notably, the definition explicitly states that any event solely attributable to these general conditions—even if it delays the consummation of the Transaction—shall be excluded from constituting an Acquisition Material Impact.

Answer the question based solely on the excerpt above.
